claim: "Petals on the Wind is a 2014 Lifetime movie sequel of the film which starred The Leftovers actress Kiernan Brennan Shipka."
evidences (the complete set of findings collected so far, oldest first):
[
 {
  "finding": {
   "question": "Is Petals on the Wind a 2014 Lifetime movie sequel of the film Flowers in the Attic?",
   "answer": "Yes, Petals on the Wind is a 2014 Lifetime movie sequel to the 2014 adaptation Flowers in the Attic.",
   "source": "Petals on the Wind (film) https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petals_on_the_Wind_(film)",
   "excerpt": "Petals on the Wind is a 2014 Lifetime movie sequel to the 2014 adaptation Flowers in the Attic, starring Heather Graham, Rose McIver, Wyatt Nash, Bailey Buntain and Ellen Burstyn.",
   "stance": "SUPPORTS"
  },
  "passage": "Title: Petals on the Wind\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petals_on_the_Wind\nExcerpt: Petals on the Wind is a novel written by V. C. Andrews in 1980. It is the second book in the Dollanganger series. The timeline takes place from the siblings' successful escape in November 1960 to the fall of 1975.  The book, like the others in the series, was a number one best-seller in North America in the early 1980s. In 2014, it was adapted into a Lifetime original movie.\n\nTitle: Flowers in the Attic (1987 film)\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flowers_in_the_Attic_(1987_film)\nExcerpt: Flowers in the Attic is a 1987 American psychological horror film directed by Jeffrey Bloom and starring Louise Fletcher, Victoria Tennant, Kristy Swanson, and Jeb Stuart Adams. Its plot follows four youngsters who, after the death of their father, are held captive in the attic of their abusive grandmother's sprawling estate by their cruel and manipulative mother. It is based on V. C. Andrews' 1979 novel of the same name.\nAt one point, Wes Craven was scheduled to direct the film, and had completed a screenplay draft. Producers were disturbed by his approach to the incest-laden story, and Jeffrey Bloom ended up with writing and directing duties.\n\nTitle: Flowers in the Attic (2014 film)\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flowers_in_the_Attic_(2014_film)\nExcerpt: Flowers in the Attic is a 2014 Lifetime psychological thriller drama movie directed by Deborah Chow. It is the second adaptation of V. C. Andrews’ 1979 novel of the same name.\nA sequel, Petals on the Wind, based on the novel of the same name, premiered on May 26, 2014, on Lifetime. The network announced the developing of the following books in the series, If There Be Thorns and Seeds of Yesterday, which both aired in 2015.\n\nTitle: Petals on the Wind (film)\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petals_on_the_Wind_(film)\nExcerpt: Petals on the Wind is a 2014 Lifetime movie sequel to the 2014 adaptation Flowers in the Attic, starring Heather Graham, Rose McIver, Wyatt Nash, Bailey Buntain and Ellen Burstyn. It is based on V. C. Andrews' 1980 novel of the same name, the second novel on the Dollanganger series. The film follows the surviving Dollanganger children—Cathy, Chris and Carrie—ten years after escaping the attic. Despite attempting to move on with their lives, after multiple failed attempts and tragedies occur, Cathy decides it is time to take revenge on her mother.\nLifetime first announced the film shortly before Flowers in the Attic was released. The network announced on the premiere of the movie the developing of the following books of the Dollanganger series, If There Be Thorns and Seeds of Yesterday, both of which aired in 2015.\nThe film received a positive response from critics.\n\nTitle: If There Be Thorns (film)\nURL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/If_There_Be_Thorns_(film)\nExcerpt: If There Be Thorns is a 2015 television film based on the best-selling 1981 novel of the same name. It premiered on April 5, 2015, and was produced by Lifetime. Seeds of Yesterday is the sequel film based on the novel of the same name."
 },
 {
  "finding": {
   "question": "Did Kiernan Brennan Shipka star in the Lifetime movie Petals on the Wind and is she known for her role in The Leftovers?",
   "answer": "INSUFFICIENT",
   "source": "",
   "excerpt": "",
   "stance": "INSUFFICIENT"
  },
  "passage": ""
 }
]

